=== D. ANTI-STUB AUDIT RATINGS ===

tools/benchmark.py — REAL.
  Calls ext/fullhouse-engine sandbox.match.run_match in-process; paired-seed
  ladder + bootstrap CIs; manifest-pinned ratchet; supports --zip artifact-bound
  mode. ~26 KB, 445 LOC of net changes vs scaffold. No constants returned.

tools/self_play.py — REAL.
  Sets up shim mount, drives sandbox.match.run_match directly. Reports
  chip_delta + bot_errors via engine output. Supports --strict.

tools/exploit_check.py — PARTIAL (documented).
  Implements a 20-spot LBR-style guard. Loads bot from packaged zip
  (`--bot submissions/X.zip`), evicts cached imports, computes per-spot
  best-response - call EV gain in mbb/g. Module docstring acknowledges
  this is an approximation of LBR (no full-game tree sim, perfect-info
  villain); the per-spot 200 mbb cap is intentional. Not a stub: it does
  invoke the loaded bot's decide().

tools/package.py — REAL.
  Builds zip from src/ + data/ with a small shim bot.py at archive root.
  --strict re-opens the zip and asserts structural invariants.

tools/import_audit.py — REAL.
  (Unchanged from scaffold; cold-imports bot.py and reports RSS.)

src/bot.py — REAL.
  Imports src.preflop_lookup, src.postflop, src.opponent_model,
  src.equity, src.sizing, src.timeout_guard. Real decide() path.

Verdict: All tools are REAL or documented PARTIAL. No evidence of fake
verification.

